BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:VJE-Seminar - Nicolas Schutz - University of Mannheim
DTSTART:20251120T121500Z
DTEND:20251120T134500Z
DTSTAMP:20251202T212445Z
UID:5ghoet3lhn1re1uad4st4e2f8k@google.com
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20250718T071106Z
DESCRIPTION:<b><u>Speaker: </u></b>Nicolas Schutz<br><br><b><u>Title: </u
 ></b>"Oligopoly\, Complementarities\, and Transformed Potentials" (jointwi
 th Volker Nocke).<br><br><b><u>Abstract:</u></b><br>We adopt a potential g
 ames approach to study multiproduct-firm pricing games.<br>We introduce th
 e new concept of transformed potential and characterize the classes<br>of 
 demand systems that give rise to pricing games admitting such a potential.
  The<br>resulting demand systems may contain nests (of closer substitutes)
  or baskets (of products<br>that are purchased jointly)\, or combinations 
 thereof. These demand systems allow<br>for flexible substitution patterns\
 , and can feature product complementarities arising<br>from joint purchase
 s and substitution away from the outside option. Combining the<br>potentia
 l games approach with a competition-in-utility approach\, we derive powerf
 ul<br>results on existence of pure-strategy Nash equilibria.<br><br><b><u>
 Webpage:</u></b> <a href="https://www.vwl.uni-mannheim.de/schutz/" target
 ="_blank">https://www.vwl.uni-mannheim.de/schutz/</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20251112T132145Z
LOCATION:HS 9\, 1. Stock 
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
